## **Layout Rationale:**

### **1. Top Bar (Persistent)**
- Game title + current Turn / Era — always visible
- Dynasty name for identity

### **2. Empire Overview Strip**
- All key resources in one glance (gold, production, science, faith, food, population, happiness)
- Summary stats (cities count, unit count)

### **3. Center — World Map**
- The biggest panel, since exploration and positioning are core to Civ-style games
- Hex grid with highlighted units, cities, and resources
- Click to select, click units to move/attack

### **4. Left Panel — Selected Object**
- Context-sensitive: shows details for whatever you click on (city, unit, district)
- Quick action buttons specific to selection (produce, build, edict, envoy)

### **5. Right Panel — Dynasty & Events**
- **Dynasty**: Monarch, traits, succession, heir, marriages (Crusader Kings DNA)
- **Recent Events**: Log of important world/city events (news ticker style)

### **6. Bottom Navigation Bar**
- **Tab bar** for jumping between major screens (Map, Cities, Units, Research, Diplomacy, Edicts, Stats)
- **Prominent "Next Turn" button** — the most important action
- **Tip line** — contextual help
- **Production queue** — always visible progress

### **7. Color Scheme (suggestion)**
- Parchment/paper background (medieval feel)
- Gold accents for dynasty elements
- Red for military, blue for science, green for food, purple for faith
- Dark borders with ornamental framing

